Overview
A government single sign-on (SSO) service is a single portal where citizens can sign on with one account for access to multiple government services via a website or mobile application. The Data field is crucial as it is essential for the system to identify users and manage their accounts correctly and securely. The system is designed by software developers, and linked to various government services. The service is easy to use on smartphones thanks to the Mobile field. Networking enables information to flow from the SSO system to other government services. Cybersecurity helps safeguard citizens' accounts and information from hackers and unauthorized use. Artificial Intelligence (AI) can be a great tool for identifying suspicious logon activity and potential security issues. Each of the six fields is essential to ensuring a safe, reliable and easy-to-use service. Effective data management also safeguards citizens' privacy and upholds the accuracy and availability of data in time.
